Talk Me Out of It uses third-party work under its own terms:

- Fonts: Geist and Geist Mono, SIL Open Font License 1.1, self-hosted from the
  @fontsource-variable/geist and @fontsource-variable/geist-mono packages.
  https://openfontlicense.org
- The model: Qwen2.5 14B by Alibaba Cloud (Apache License 2.0), run locally
  through Ollama (MIT). The saved debates in sessions/gallery/ are its output.
  The model itself is not part of this repository.
- Libraries bundled into the site: React and React DOM (MIT), Motion (MIT),
  Lucide (ISC), clsx (MIT), and Tailwind CSS (MIT), which produces the
  stylesheet. Build and deploy tools, none of which reach
  visitors: Vite (MIT), TypeScript (Apache-2.0), and Wrangler (MIT or
  Apache-2.0).
- The engine: the Ollama Python client (MIT) and Pydantic (MIT).
- Design: the look of the site adapts ideas from components published on
  21st.dev, rewritten against this project's own colors and type. Three carry
  an MIT license, and the license notices they came with are kept in the
  files in ui/pulled/: Tweenly Chart KPI (mirukullacode), Klyv Shimmer Button
  (Klyv contributors), and Feature Grid Spotlight Cards (Mohammad Shehadeh,
  from Hirael). Seven others arrived with no license text: Illuminated Hero
  (efferd), Chat Messages (nexus-ui), Typing Indicator (ddoemonn), Chat Bubble
  Reactions (bundui), User Presence Avatar (adrielzimbril), LiquidAurora
  (dhileepkumargm), and Agent Trace (n1m4mz). So did the three themes
  considered, and the Darkmatter theme (serafimcloud) whose color values the
  site's tokens adapt. Those files were reviewed and are not in this
  repository; ui/pulled/REVIEW.md records what each one was and what the review
  found. If you are an author and want a credit changed or removed, write to
  hello@icarianforge.com.
